<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adolphe Thiers</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1797">1797</a>–<a href="/years/1877">1877</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adolphe Thiers was a French historian and statesman who served as a minister and prime minister under the July Monarchy. After the defeat by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> he became head of the executive in 1871, made peace and sent the army to crush the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> Commune in May 1871. As first president of the Third Republic he paid off the war indemnity before resigning in 1873.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adolphe-thiers.jpg" alt="Adolphe Thiers" width="320" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nadar · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adolphe_Thiers_Nadar_2.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
